{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/snowplowencoding"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"externalID":"SnowplowEncoding","roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","modules":[{"name":"SnowplowEncoding"}],"title":"SnowplowEncoding","symbolKind":"module"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:backoff:clock:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" makes an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":") for a Snowplow pipeline in one call. It checks the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"collector’s URL, the Iglu vendor and the app ID, and posts to the collector’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/com.snowplowanalytics.snowplow\/tp2"},{"type":"text","text":" endpoint with a "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":". It splits each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"batch to the limits of Snowplow’s own mobile trackers ("},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"): 25"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events and 40,000 bytes a request, with a larger event, of up to 150,000 bytes, in a request of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its own. A batch with no record the encoder can write, an empty one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"included, makes no request. The destination retries no response, a 5xx, 408 and 429, and drops"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and reports any other status. No trace context is sent. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":" leaves this module out;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"import it on its own."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A collector takes events from anyone who can reach it, so there is no key or secret, and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destination builds on every platform: an app sends to the collector directly."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import HTTPDestinations","import SnowplowEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let snowplow = try HTTPDestination.snowplow(","    collector: collector,  \/\/ https:\/\/collector.example.com","    vendor: \"com.example\",  \/\/ the Iglu vendor the plan is exported under","    appID: \"shop-ios\",","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: snowplow)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The factory throws ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowSetupError"},{"text":" for a collector URL that isn’t ","type":"text"},{"code":"https","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", that has no host,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a user name, a query or a fragment, or that already ends in the endpoint; for a vendor Iglu","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"doesn’t take; and for an empty app ID or one longer than 255 UTF-16 code units.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Schemas-from-the-tracking-plan","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Schemas from the tracking plan"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each event is a self-describing event: its data comes with the Iglu URI of the schema it must"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"match, and Snowplow’s pipeline validates it against that schema before loading it. The URI is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"named after the event and its version, under the vendor the destination is given:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["iglu:<vendor>\/<name>\/jsonschema\/<version>-0-0"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":null},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Version N of an event is SchemaVer ","type":"text"},{"code":"N-0-0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and events always name it. Raising an event’s version","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is a breaking change, which is SchemaVer’s MODEL. The export compares each event with the newest","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"schema of its version the registry holds, by what the two mean rather than their bytes, as the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"plan’s own check does:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An event that hasn’t changed keeps its published file, and nothing is written."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A breaking change at the same version, such as a property made required, is refused: raise the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event’s version."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A compatible change, such as an optional property added, is an ADDITION. For Iglu Server the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"export writes it as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"N-0-1"},{"type":"text","text":", then "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"N-0-2"},{"type":"text","text":", each listing the earlier ones in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$supersedes"},{"type":"text","text":", and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Snowplow validates events naming "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"N-0-0"},{"type":"text","text":" against the newest, so a release already in users’"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hands keeps validating. Superseding needs Iglu Server 0.11.0 or later and Enrich 3.8.0 or later."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A static repository doesn’t support it: it would validate those events against "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"N-0-0"},{"type":"text","text":" alone,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so for one the export refuses the change, and the event needs a new version."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Write the registry from the plan with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan.writeIgluRegistry(to:vendor:registry:)"},{"type":"text","text":", the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"iglu <vendor> server|static <registry-directory>"},{"type":"text","text":" command of the tracking plan’s executable, or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"export-tracking-plan"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"--iglu-vendor"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"--iglu-registry"},{"type":"text","text":". Then publish it with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"igluctl"},{"type":"text","text":" before the release that sends the events."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An event name Iglu takes holds only ASCII letters, digits, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_"},{"type":"text","text":", and the version must be 1"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or more. The encoder skips every record of an event that breaks either rule, and logs a notice for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each such event of the plan when the destination is made. The export refuses such an event too."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"What-Snowplow-receives","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"What Snowplow receives"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each request is a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"payload_data"},{"type":"text","text":" 1-0-4 array of events, one per record. Every event has:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"e"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ue"},{"text":": a self-describing event, with its data in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ue_pr"},{"text":" as JSON text;","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"eid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the record’s identifier, which a redelivered record keeps;","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"dtm","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"ttm","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the record’s timestamp in milliseconds, so Snowplow’s "},{"code":"derived_tstamp","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is when"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the event was tracked;"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"aid"},{"text":", the app ID; ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"text":", the platform; ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tv"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"traffluent"},{"text":"; and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ip"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0.0.0.0"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"No ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"stm"},{"text":" is sent: a retried request sends the same body again, so a sent time would be the first","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attempt’s, and Snowplow would move the event later by however long the retries took.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The standard context, when the record has it, goes in ","type":"text"},{"code":"co","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as Snowplow’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"mobile_context","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" 1-0-3","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(the operating system, Apple as the manufacturer, the device model, the network type and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"language) and ","type":"text"},{"code":"application","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" 1-0-0 (the app’s version and build). The platform is ","type":"text"},{"code":"mob","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for a phone,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pad, watch or Vision Pro, ","type":"text"},{"code":"tv","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for an Apple TV, ","type":"text"},{"code":"pc","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for a Mac and ","type":"text"},{"code":"app","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for a record with no device.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"type":"text","text":" the encoder is made with. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Only-the-session-identifies-a-record","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Only the session identifies a record"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The record’s session, from the sessions enricher, is its ","type":"text"},{"code":"sid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", Snowplow’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"domain_sessionid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nothing else identifies it. No ","type":"text"},{"code":"duid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"uid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"nuid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"tnuid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is sent, no ","type":"text"},{"code":"client_session","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"entity (its ","type":"text"},{"code":"userId","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" lasts across sessions), and no IDFV, IDFA or other device identifier. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record’s vendor identifier and trace context aren’t sent either. A record with no session, from a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tracker without the sessions enricher, is sent without a ","type":"text"},{"code":"sid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; a record a store recovered after a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"relaunch keeps its session and its ","type":"text"},{"code":"sid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Snowplow’s mobile data models","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"read a session from the ","type":"text"},{"code":"client_session","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" entity, so set the unified package’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"snowplow__session_identifiers","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to ","type":"text"},{"code":"[{\"schema\": \"atomic\", \"field\": \"domain_sessionid\"}]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for these","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"events.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The collector would give each device an identifier of its own: it sets an "},{"code":"sp","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" cookie, which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"URLSession","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps and sends back, and records the request’s IP address. Every request carries"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"SP-Anonymous: *","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so the collector sets and reads no cookie, records "},{"code":"network_userid","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" as all"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"zeros, and records no IP address or forwarding header fields."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Records-left-out","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Records left out"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out and the rest of the batch is sent:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"one the plan doesn’t describe, whose event isn’t ","type":"text"},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or that holds a value JSON can’t;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"one whose event name Iglu doesn’t take, or whose version is below 1;","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose timestamp falls outside the years 0 to 9999, which Snowplow’s enrichment fails;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose JSON is over 150,000 bytes, which the smallest of a pipeline’s streams, SQS’s 192 kB,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"might not take with the request around it."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The destination reports each as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":" whose reason is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowEncodingError","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"What-the-collector-doesnt-report","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"What the collector doesn’t report"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The collector answers 200 to every request it can read and validates nothing. Snowplow checks the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events later, in enrichment. An event whose data its schema rejects, whose schema the pipeline’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Iglu resolver can’t find, or that is larger than the pipeline’s stream takes, becomes a failed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event: it is kept apart and never reaches the warehouse, though the destination counted it as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivered. Publish each schema before the release that sends it, and watch the pipeline’s failed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events after a change to the plan. Snowplow’s resolver caches schemas, for 10 minutes by default,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so a schema published after the first event that names it can still be missed for that long."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Snowplow doesn’t remove duplicates as events arrive. A record is sent more than once when a request"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is retried after the collector stored it but the answer was lost, when a delivery sends a cancelled"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"batch again, and when a store redelivers records after a relaunch. Each copy keeps its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"eid"},{"type":"text","text":", so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Snowplow’s data models, which deduplicate on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"event_id"},{"type":"text","text":", count it once."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers what Snowplow receives, and why, in more detail."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Sending to Snowplow","anchor":"Sending-to-Snowplow","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowSetupError"]},{"title":"Encoding batches","anchor":"Encoding-batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder"]},{"title":"Records left out","anchor":"Records-left-out","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowEncodingError"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Send records to a Snowplow collector as self-describing events, whose schemas come from the tracking plan.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://SnowplowEncoding/documentation/SnowplowEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:backoff:clock:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/snowplowencoding\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination\/snowplow(collector:vendor:appid:plan:backoff:clock:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:backoff:clock:)","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"snowplow","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"collector","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"URL","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:20FoundationEssentials3URLV"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"vendor","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"appID","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"plan","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TrackingPlan","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:13TrackingPlans0A4PlanV"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"backoff","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ExponentialBackoff","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations18ExponentialBackoffV"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"clock","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Clock","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency5ClockP"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Duration","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV"},{"text":">) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"SnowplowSetupError","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16SnowplowEncoding0A10SetupErrorO"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"HTTPDestination","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations15HTTPDestinationV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"URLSessionTransport","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations19URLSessionTransportV"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SnowplowBatchEncoder","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16SnowplowEncoding0A12BatchEncoderV"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A destination that sends batches to the Snowplow collector at ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"collector"},{"text":", as self-describing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"events whose schemas are ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"text":"’s under ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vendor"},{"text":", from the app ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"appID"},{"text":", with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSession.shared"},{"text":", retrying a send that fails for now with the waits of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"backoff"},{"text":" on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clock"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:backoff:clock:)","conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Transport"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSessionTransport"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encoding"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SnowplowBatchEncoder"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}},"doc://SnowplowEncoding/documentation/SnowplowEncoding/SnowplowBatchEncoder/init(vendor:appID:plan:limit:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder\/init(vendor:appID:plan:limit:)","url":"\/documentation\/snowplowencoding\/snowplowbatchencoder\/init(vendor:appid:plan:limit:)","type":"topic","title":"init(vendor:appID:plan:limit:)","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An encoder of the events "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"type":"text","text":" describes, whose schemas are under "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vendor"},{"type":"text","text":", sent as the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"app "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"appID"},{"type":"text","text":", splitting each batch to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"limit"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"vendor"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdenti